          "tz": 0
        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "patrick bot",
          "email": "patrick-bot@mulberrytree.us",
          "date": "2026-11-06 02:36:51.000000000",
          "tz": 0
        },
        "subject": "LU-20076 tests: stop a target with one remote command",
        "message": "LU-20076 tests: stop a target with one remote command\n\nStopping a target cost three remote commands: a check that\nit is mounted, the umount, and the wait for devices in the\nST state, which polls with one more command each time. With\ndm-flakey enabled (the default) a fourth checks for module\nsupport on every stop. A ZFS target adds the pool export,\nand where the dm-flakey device is removed (a failover pair,\nCLEANUP_DM_DEV, or a second file system) the removal adds\nmore.\n\nRun all of this as one remote script. The wait for the ST\ndevices runs on the server, with the same intervals and\nlimit, and wait_exit_ST() also uses that script. Messages\nare the same as before, but they are printed when the script\nends rather than as it runs, so the progress of a long wait\nshows only at its end. The dm-flakey support check now runs\nonly where the device is removed.\n\nThe return code is that of the remote script. If the remote\ncommand itself fails (the server is unreachable or dies\nduring the umount), stop() now returns that failure, where\nit used to return 0; callers that check it, and stopall, can\nfail where they passed before.\n\nMeasured on a cluster of one MDS with 4 MDTs, one OSS with 6\nOSTs and 2 clients, median of 3 to 6 runs, as is and with\n0.25 s added to each remote command (command counts are for\nFLAKEY=false; with the default an ldiskfs stop was 4 -> 1):\n\n                cmds       as is           +0.25 s\n  stop ost1    3 -> 1   0.29 -> 0.12 s  1.00 -> 0.35 s\n  stop mds2    3 -> 1   0.34 -> 0.23 s  1.09 -> 0.47 s\n  stopall     34 -> 14  22.5 -> 21.3 s  23.9 -> 23.5 s\n\nstopall's time is mostly an umount wait in the kernel. CI\nstops about 8.5 million targets in 30 days; at least two\nfewer commands of 0.2 to 0.35 s each, counting a parallel\nstop as half, is roughly 430 to 1240 hours of test time, more\non configurations with failover partners.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=conf-sanity,replay-single\nTest-Parameters: trivial fstype=zfs testlist=conf-sanity\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=insanity,recovery-small\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5\nSigned-off-by: Patrick Farrell <patrick@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: I4d848dd48f029be2ebc13b97f9537b829ffa334a\n"
      },
